  "body": "Found in the review of PR #2323 (issue #2317). None of these items gives wrong output today.\n\n1. `crates/motion/src/machining2d/arc_touch.rs:82-90`: with one NaN end, the NaN guard at line 86 does not fire. Non-finite chords are not sent there today. Add an explicit finite check at the start of `grazes`.\n2. `arc_touch.rs:58`: the reach calculation skips a NaN bracket point, so a touch could be made from such a bracket. The bracket code does not make one today. Refuse a bracket with a non-finite point.\n3. The `TOUCH` bound (1e-5 mm) is pinned only by the two `arc_touch` unit tests. Add an end-to-end fixture: a chord 1e-3 mm inside the end tangent of a corner arc must be a crossing in the emitted pocket.\n4. `docs/decisions/2317-blend-crossing-law.md` says \"the unrounded pass\" for the fallback after 3 rounds. Some fitted arcs stay chords there. Correct the wording.\n\nDone means: items 1 to 3 have tests that fail without the change, and item 4 is corrected.\n",
